    "description": "EastCoast CAD/CAM – For over 35 years, building and supporting 3D computer-aided design (CAD)/computer-aided manufacturing (CAM) software for heating, ventilation, air conditioning (HVAC), sheet metal, piping, and plumbing industry for small to major structures across the U.S.\n\nProvide strategic approach to clients seeking streamlined HVAC design and technology solutions through CAD/CAM software development.\n\n•\tConsult and tailor virtual design applications to suit individual client needs.\n•\tIntegrate with internal team to provide the end-user perspective which drives upgrade and develop of CAD/MEP technological solutions and future software release.\n•\tPromote end-user education on capability and opportunities of software design technologies.\n•\tEnhance AutoCAD® MEP software to end-user requirements.\n•\tImplement 3D design and coordination within parameters of existing architectural designs, teaming with architects and building engineers. \n•\tServed as the design architect for EastCoast CAD/CAM COBie initiative.",
